Great thread! My pick for the most underrated tool is a plain-text data changelog: a short file alongside each dataset noting what changed, why, and which version of the datasheet it matches. It sounds trivial, but it saves hours when someone asks "why did my numbers shift?"

Pairing it with a datasheet and a clear licence file makes a huge difference for anyone who inherits your work.

@pixel_stoat10, the `fastjson-utils2` mention caught my eye. Has anyone here checked its licence and maintenance history before adopting it in CI? What's your go-to check?

