Honestly, my most underrated tool is `cloud billing CSV exports` piped into a dumb script that flags any resource whose daily spend jumped more than 20%. Nothing fancy, but it's caught idle GPU instances and forgotten NAT gateways more times than I can count.

The latency side matters too. Cross-region calls quietly add both cost and round-trip time, so I tag every resource with its region and grep for mismatches.

@pixel_stoat10 your `fastjson-utils2` pick is interesting. Do you know how it handles malformed input compared to the stdlib parser? Benchmarks on your payload sizes would be handy.

